tring')}\nbereavement/grief examples 30\n\n ('clinical', 'grief', 'Bereavement (death of loved one)', 86, \"The kitchen counter still had the grocery list in his handwriting. Bananas, milk, the kind of bread she never liked. She opened the refrigerator and found the leftovers he'd portioned into containers, labeled with days of the week. Thursday\")\n\n ('clinical', 'grief', 'Bereavement (death of loved one)', 78, 'The woman at the front desk asked her to sign for his personal effects. A watch. A wallet with eleven dollars. A bus pass that expired next month. She put them in her coat pocket, where they made almost no weight at all. Outside, the parkin')\n\n ('clinical', 'grief', 'Bereavement (death of loved one)', 89, 'His daughter had stopped answering the phone in complete sentences. When he called, she would say \"yeah\" or \"okay\" or nothing. The school sent a letter about attendance. He found the dog sitting by the back door again, in the same spot, fac')\n\n ('clinical', 'grief', 'Bereavement (death of loved one)', 95, \"They told her she could take the room whenever she was ready. She wasn't ready. She went in anyway. The sheets were still pressed into the shape of the body that had been there. A glass of water on the nightstand, half-finished. The televis\")\n\n ('clinical', 'grief', \"Career destruction (life's work lost)\", 91, 'The lab was empty now. Twenty-two years of research. The server room had been cleared by facilities before she\\'d arrived Monday morning. The backup drives weren\\'t in the cabinet. She found a single Post-it note on the monitor: \"Assets trans')\n\n ('clinical', 'grief', \"Career destruction (life's work lost)\", 100, 'The carpenter ran his hand along the doorframe of the shop. Thirty-one years. The auction company had tagged everything — the table saw, the planer, the chisels his father had given him, each one with a yellow sticker and a lot number. Some')\n\n ('clinical', 'grief', \"Career destruction (life's work lost)\", 94,